<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<aiml version="2.0">

  <category>
    <pattern>REVISIONS</pattern>
    <template>Every commission includes up to 3 rounds of revisions at no extra charge. This covers lyric changes, structural edits, tempo adjustments, and style refinements. Additional revision rounds beyond the 3 included are available at $25 per round.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>REVISION POLICY</pattern>
    <template>Our revision policy: every commission includes 3 rounds of revisions at no extra charge. Additional rounds are $25 each. Major directional changes after production has begun may be quoted separately.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HOW MANY REVISIONS</pattern>
    <template>Every commission includes up to 3 rounds of revisions at no extra cost. If you need more after that, additional rounds are available at $25 each.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>CAN I MAKE CHANGES</pattern>
    <template>Absolutely. We include 3 revision rounds with every commission — you can request lyric changes, structural edits, tempo adjustments, and more. If you need additional rounds beyond those 3, they're available at $25 each.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF I DO NOT LIKE THE SONG</pattern>
    <template>That is what revisions are for. You get 3 rounds of changes included, so we can refine the song until it truly reflects your vision. If you have a very specific direction, sharing reference tracks or detailed notes during your inquiry helps us nail it faster.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF I WANT CHANGES</pattern>
    <template>No problem — that is the revision process. Every commission includes 3 rounds of changes. You review our draft, send your feedback, and we revise. We keep going until you love it (within those 3 rounds).</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>EXTRA REVISIONS</pattern>
    <template>If you need more than the 3 included revision rounds, additional rounds are $25 each. Just let us know and we'll keep refining until it's perfect.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HOW DO REVISIONS WORK</pattern>
    <template>After we deliver the first draft, you review it and send detailed feedback. We incorporate your notes and deliver a revised version. This cycle repeats up to 3 times at no extra cost. After that, additional rounds are $25 each.</template>
  </category>

  <!-- ── Refund policy ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->

  <category>
    <pattern>DO YOU OFFER REFUNDS</pattern>
    <template>We don't offer refunds once production is underway — but that's exactly why we include three rounds of revisions at no extra charge. Our goal is to make the song genuinely right for you, and we keep working until it is. If you have concerns at any stage, reach out and we'll address them directly.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IS YOUR REFUND POLICY</pattern>
    <template><srai>DO YOU OFFER REFUNDS</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>CAN I GET A REFUND</pattern>
    <template><srai>DO YOU OFFER REFUNDS</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>MONEY BACK GUARANTEE</pattern>
    <template><srai>DO YOU OFFER REFUNDS</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>MONEY BACK</pattern>
    <template><srai>DO YOU OFFER REFUNDS</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF I AM NOT SATISFIED</pattern>
    <template>Your satisfaction is why every commission includes three revision rounds — we revise until the song truly reflects your vision. If at any point you're concerned about the direction, reach out directly and we'll make it right.
      <quick-replies><reply>How many revisions do I get?</reply><reply>How do revisions work?</reply></quick-replies>
    </template>
  </category>

  <!-- ── Revision widening ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->

  <category>
    <pattern>DO YOU DO UNLIMITED REVISIONS</pattern>
    <template>We include three revision rounds with every commission at no extra charge — that covers the vast majority of refinements. If you need more, additional rounds are available at $25 each. We find that with clear feedback and our discovery process, three rounds is more than enough to get the song exactly right.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HOW MANY ROUNDS OF REVISIONS</pattern>
    <template><srai>HOW MANY REVISIONS</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HOW MANY TIMES CAN I MAKE CHANGES</pattern>
    <template><srai>HOW MANY REVISIONS</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>CAN I REQUEST CHANGES</pattern>
    <template><srai>CAN I MAKE CHANGES</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>CAN I CHANGE THE LYRICS</pattern>
    <template><srai>CAN I MAKE CHANGES</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>CAN I CHANGE THE GENRE</pattern>
    <template><srai>CAN I MAKE CHANGES</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>CAN I CHANGE THE STYLE</pattern>
    <template><srai>CAN I MAKE CHANGES</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF I WANT SOMETHING DIFFERENT</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IF I DO NOT LIKE THE SONG</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF I HATE IT</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IF I DO NOT LIKE THE SONG</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF I AM UNHAPPY</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IF I DO NOT LIKE THE SONG</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF I DO NOT LIKE IT</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IF I DO NOT LIKE THE SONG</srai></template>
  </category>

  <!-- ── Gift recipient / third-party anxiety ──────────────────────────────── -->

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF MY PARTNER DOES NOT LIKE IT</pattern>
    <template>That's a completely natural concern when the song is a surprise gift. Share specific details about their taste when you submit — favorite styles, artists they love, songs that move them — and we'll build toward something that resonates. If the first draft still feels off, the revision rounds let you refine it before the moment arrives.
      <quick-replies><reply>How many revisions do I get?</reply><reply>Can I provide a reference track?</reply></quick-replies>
    </template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF THEY DO NOT LIKE THE SONG</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IF MY PARTNER DOES NOT LIKE IT</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF THE RECIPIENT DOES NOT LIKE IT</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IF MY PARTNER DOES NOT LIKE IT</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF THEY HATE THE SONG</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IF MY PARTNER DOES NOT LIKE IT</srai></template>
  </category>

  <!-- ── First draft anxiety ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF THE FIRST DRAFT IS COMPLETELY WRONG</pattern>
    <template>That's what revision rounds are for. If the first draft misses the mark entirely, treat your feedback as a reset rather than a refinement — tell us specifically what didn't work and what you needed instead, and we'll approach the second draft with fresh direction. The discovery call before production helps minimize that risk, but if it happens, we'll address it directly.
      <quick-replies><reply>How many revisions do I get?</reply><reply>What is a discovery call?</reply></quick-replies>
    </template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF THE FIRST VERSION IS NOT RIGHT</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IF THE FIRST DRAFT IS COMPLETELY WRONG</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF THE FIRST DRAFT IS OFF</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IF THE FIRST DRAFT IS COMPLETELY WRONG</srai></template>
  </category>

  <!-- ── Major direction change ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF I CHANGE MY MIND COMPLETELY</pattern>
    <template>Major directional changes after production has begun may require a separate conversation depending on how far along we are — but we'll always work through it with you directly rather than deliver something that doesn't fit. If you're still working out the vision, the discovery call is the right place to get there before the writing starts.
      <nav-card label="Get in Touch" href="/contact"/>
    </template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF I COMPLETELY CHANGE MY MIND</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IF I CHANGE MY MIND COMPLETELY</srai></template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF MY STORY CHANGES</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IF I CHANGE MY MIND COMPLETELY</srai></template>
  </category>

  <!-- ── "Will it sound different from what I imagined?" ───────────────────── -->

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF IT SOUNDS TOTALLY DIFFERENT FROM WHAT I WANTED</pattern>
    <template>That's exactly why we include three revision rounds and why the discovery call matters. The more clearly you describe the emotional target and share reference tracks upfront, the closer our first draft lands. If there's still a gap, we address it in revisions — and we don't stop until the song is genuinely right.
      <quick-replies><reply>How many revisions do I get?</reply><reply>Can I provide a reference track?</reply></quick-replies>
    </template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IF IT IS NOT WHAT I EXPECTED</pattern>
    <template><srai>WHAT IF IT SOUNDS TOTALLY DIFFERENT FROM WHAT I WANTED</srai></template>
  </category>

</aiml>
